---
import Docs from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import TableWrap from '../../../components/TableWrap.astro';
import Code from '../../../components/Code.astro';
const toc = [{ id: 'path', text: 'The path for anything new' }, { id: 'checks', text: 'What the build checks' }, { id: 'run', text: 'Run the checks' }, { id: 'versioning', text: 'Versioning' }];
const runCode = `npm run build          # tokens, contrast, usage, parity
cd docs && npm ci && npm run build && npm run verify`;
---
<Docs title="Contributing" crumb="Guides" lead="How a token or component gets into Flint, and what has to pass before it ships." toc={toc}>
  <h2 id="path">The path for anything new</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>File an ASDS ticket</strong> describing the need.</li>
    <li><strong>Reuse first.</strong> Build only when no token or component fits.</li>
    <li><strong>Tokens first.</strong> Add or change tokens before touching a component.</li>
    <li><strong>Every state,</strong> with an accessibility note.</li>
    <li><strong>Add it to the workbench</strong> (<code>docs/src/workbench/benches.jsx</code>) and walk it: every state, light and dark, both densities, keyboard only.</li>
    <li><strong>Document it here:</strong> usage, style, code and accessibility.</li>
    <li><strong>Release:</strong> bump the version, add a changelog entry, tag it.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="checks">What the build checks</h2>
  <TableWrap label="Build checks">
    <table class="data">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Fails when</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Contrast</th><td>A text pair drops under 7:1, or a control edge, focus ring or chart color under 3:1, in either mode.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Usage</th><td>A control is drawn with a decorative border, or a density shrinks a control or target.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Parity</th><td>CSS, MUI, shadcn or Swift lands on a value tokens.json didn't give it, or the MUI theme hardcodes a color.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Docs and workbench</th><td>Any axe violation on any page, light or dark (workbench pages at both densities); a blocked script or style; sideways scroll at phone width; focus not landing and holding on headings; a workbench Hover row that looks like Default; or a semantic or component token with no row in the docs.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableWrap>

  <h2 id="run">Run the checks</h2>
  <Code label="Terminal" code={runCode} />

  <h2 id="versioning">Versioning</h2>
  <p>Flint uses semver, separate from the apps that use it. A new token or component is a minor. A value fix is a patch. A rename or removal is a major. Deprecated tokens keep working for one minor release, then go in the next major.</p>
</Docs>
